 "note": "x/y/w/h are pixels within the sheet, checked against a render. Water: stream_* tiles for 1-wide streams, pond for a 3x3 pond. footprint = the tiles an entity occupies for collision and pushing, in tiles, anchored at the sprite's bottom-left tile; optional x is a column offset from that tile (default 0). Sprites without one occupy 1x1. Tall trees/rocks block only their bottom row so the player can walk behind the canopy. offset {x,y} is an optional pixel nudge applied when drawing. layer: ground (flat, under everything), object (y-sorted with the player), above (drawn over objects), overlay (whole screen); terrain tiles have no layer. anims: named frame ranges {from,to,fps?,loop?} in a strip; the player instead uses rows (dirs are columns) and poses [col,row]. pieces: true means each frame is a separate particle piece, pick one, do not animate. materials: what it is made of, main material first; mixed things list several. variants: related sprites by name, the same map on every member; becomes: what this turns into after an event.",
